  "summary": "The Cheyenne County (CO) Sheriff's Office announced it will continue using Flock license-plate reader cameras after a trial period that began in January 2026. The release describes six cameras, claimed investigative successes, a 30-day retention window, and 60-day audits.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "In January 2026, the Cheyenne County Sheriff's Office began utilizing FLOCK License Plate Reader (LPR) cameras on a trial basis as an additional investigative and public safety tool.",
      "paragraph_idx": 2
    },
    {
      "quote": "Data is stored for 30 days, unless it is flagged for an active investigation.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "the use of FLOCK cameras is audited every 60 days to ensure compliance with policy, appropriate use, and continued effectiveness",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    }
